  "notes": "West leads the ♦K against 6♥. The only possible problem is a 4-1 trump break. In that case, South must try to establish the dummy, ruffing 2 of North's diamonds and discarding North's remaining diamond and club losers on South's spades.\n\nWest's diamond lead should be ducked in the dummy and ruffed by South. The ♥A and ♥Q are cashed. When West discards on the second round of trump, South must play carefully.\n\nSouth crosses in spades and leads another diamond, ruffing in the closed hand. South tries to cross again in spades. East cannot afford to ruff as the North and South hands still have a link in spades.\n\nWhen East discards, the ♥K can be cashed. A heart trick is conceded to East. North's ♦A and ♣A can handle any return East makes. South will be able to run his spades without any worry of East ruffing in.",
  "commentary_paragraphs": [
